      "writtenOn": "2024-09-12T20:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is somewhat contrived. Sink Caps shall always contain one 5V fixed PDO. It would be reasonable for us to disregard this sink caps message without ever having evaluated the voltage/current. Maybe we want to test the case of an invalid Sink Caps, but another, separate case would be a fixed 5V/1.5A followed by a variable 5V/3A (still a little silly, but valid).",
